  "answer": "`src/refund-settlement/status.ts` accepts four processing states and publishes one frame. I couldn't read `tea-rags://guide/freshness`. The tool that reads MCP resources, `ReadMcpResourceTool`, is blocked by a hook that only allows tea-rags tool discovery. I answered from the tea-rags core freshness rules and the file's current contents instead.\n\n**Accepted states**\n\nThe `ProcessingState` type at `src/refund-settlement/status.ts:1` is a union of `\"queued\" | \"processing\" | \"settled\" | \"rejected\"`. `applyProcessingState(record, state, publish)` takes that type as its `state` argument. It doesn't validate or restrict transitions. It writes whatever state it gets to `record.processingState`.\n\n**Published frame**\n\nRight after the assignment, the function calls `publish` with this object:\n\n```ts\n{\n  resource: { id: record.refundId, processing_status: record.processingState },\n  type: \"refund_settlement\",\n  event: \"status_changed\",\n}\n```\n\n- **Resource:** it carries `id`, which is the refund ID, and `processing_status`, which is the new state. The field name is snake_case here, while the record field is `processingState`.\n- **Type and event:** `type` is `\"refund_settlement\"` and `event` is `\"status_changed\"`.\n- **Typing:** the `publish` callback is typed `(frame: object) => void`, so the frame shape isn't enforced by the type system.\n- **Purpose:** the doc comment says these updates go to the operations dashboard.\n\n**Freshness**\n\nThe result row had no `treeState` or `degraded` marker, so I treated it as current. The response reported 3 pending files across the project, but none of them is flagged against this file. I didn't reindex.",
